1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,010
When looking at Western Europe, we don't usually think about poverty – but in fact, some people in modern-day Britain are so hard up that they can't afford to buy food.
当我们审视西欧时，通常不会想到贫困——但实际上，现如今一些英国人经济拮据，以至于买不起食物。

2
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:17,650
Back in 2008, the financial crisis caused a lot of redundancies.
早在2008年，金融危机导致了许多人被裁员。

3
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:25,560
Then there were the cuts to the welfare system in 2013 which added to the problem – and many British people fell into debt.
然后是2013年福利制度的削减，这加剧了问题——许多英国人负债累累。

4
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:32,820
It's estimated that 500,000 people in the UK have turned to food banks, just to get by.
据估计，英国有50万人求助于食品银行，只为勉强维持生计。

5
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:41,000
Steph Hagen, who works in a Nottingham food bank, says: "People do not go to a food bank because it's an open door.
在诺丁汉食品银行工作的斯蒂芬·哈根说：“人们去食品银行并不是因为它敞开大门。

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,450
It's a case of they go to it because they need to.
而是因为他们不得不去。

7
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:53,550
With our food bank – we are an independent one, and we have limited stocks – everyone who comes through our door has no income whatsoever."
我们的食品银行是独立的，库存有限——每个来我们这里的人都没有任何收入。”

8
00:00:53,550 --> 00:00:58,530
There are checks and referrals to make sure nobody is abusing the system.
检查和推荐机制确保没有人滥用该系统。

9
00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:06,900
If a doctor or a social worker thinks someone needs to use a food bank – even for a short time – they can give them vouchers.
如果医生或社工认为某人需要使用食品银行——即使是短期的——他们可以给他们发放代金券。

10
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:13,880
Then the people in need take the vouchers along to the food bank and they get handouts for three days.
然后，有需要的人带着代金券去食品银行，领取三天的救济品。

11
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:18,560
Churches and individual donors provide most of the food in the banks.
教堂和个人捐赠者提供了食品银行的大部分食物。

12
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:21,850
But some businesses might help out too.
但一些企业也可能提供帮助。

13
00:01:21,850 --> 00:01:25,010
And what sort of food is offered in food banks?
食品银行提供什么样的食物？

14
00:01:25,010 --> 00:01:28,650
Hagen says: "Basically, we've got porridge.
哈根说：“基本上，我们有粥。

15
00:01:28,650 --> 00:01:34,920
We do occasionally get fresh produce but it's very rare, especially in the winter months.
我们偶尔会得到新鲜农产品，但这非常罕见，尤其是在冬季。

16
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:38,330
It's like, tinned fruit, tinned ready meals.
比如罐头水果、罐头即食餐。

17
00:01:38,330 --> 00:01:45,090
We have to give out 'no-cooking' food parcels because people can't afford the gas and electricity".
我们必须分发‘无需烹饪’的食品包裹，因为人们负担不起煤气和电费。”

18
00:01:45,090 --> 00:01:49,200
Community spirit has a lot to do with food banks.
社区精神与食品银行有很大关系。

19
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:54,340
Volunteers say they are a great meeting place for people who are lonely and depressed.
志愿者们说，食品银行是孤独和沮丧的人们一个很好的聚集地。

20
00:01:54,340 --> 00:02:02,180
And when facing a crisis, some beneficiaries might need to feed not only their belly – but also their soul.
而在面对危机时，一些受益者可能不仅需要填饱肚子——还需要抚慰心灵。
